  Are you a blogger or a publisher looking to monetize your content but still not sure about how to get **Google AdSense approval**? Look no further. Our guide covers the step-by-step process and tips to avoid getting banned on AdSense.
  
  With over [40 million](https://onehourprofessor.com/google-adsense-statistics-and-data/) websites live with Google AdSense, it is one of the best methods for publishers to monetize their content. However, getting approved by Google AdSense is not a plain-sailing task.
  
  Google AdSense approval requires adherence to [Google’s strict policies](https://support.google.com/adsense/answer/48182?hl=en). Specifically, in the world of content creation, publishers need to maintain high-quality and original content, plus understand Google’s approval criteria before applying for AdSense. In this blog, we’ll explore why publishers need AdSense approval and some tips and tricks to get fast AdSense approval.
  
  Table of Contents:
  
  [Toggle](https://www.adpushup.com/blog/google-adsense-approval/#)
  
  ## Why Publishers Prefer Google AdSense?
  
  There are several available [options for monetizing your website](https://www.adpushup.com/blog/google-adsense-alternatives/), leaving you to ponder whether or not Google AdSense reigns supreme. [Google AdSense](https://www.adpushup.com/google-adsense/) is an advertising platform that allows content creators to make money through ads. These ads are provided by advertisers or brands who pay money to advertise through AdSense. But here’s the deal: you may now have to go through certain trials and tribulations to get your Google AdSense approval.
  
  When a publisher’s content displays an ad through AdSense, Google recognizes revenue and pays out [68%](https://www.cnbc.com/2021/05/18/how-does-google-make-money-advertising-business-breakdown-.html) of that [revenue to the publisher](https://www.adpushup.com/blog/google-adsense-revenue/).
  
  Google AdSense has more than [40 million](https://trends.builtwith.com/websitelist/Google-Adsense) websites using it, and that’s not all; there are plenty of advantages to using it. Take a look:
  
  - Easy to Set Up
  - Manage multiple websites with a single AdSense account
  - No need for traffic for Approval
  - Popular for its CPC terms
  
  And the list goes on.
  
  ## 7 Tips to Get Fast AdSense Approval
  
  Securing Google AdSense approval quickly requires content that ensures quality, compliance, and optimization. Always make sure that your website is well prepared and has optimal site performance to speed up the approval process. Here is a checklist of 7 insightful tips to fast-track your AdSense approval process. Let’s explore:
  
  ### 1\. Meet the Criteria
  
  Even before you apply for Google AdSense, your website should be in adherence to AdSense Policies. The website should reflect a clear vision and purpose of the website through original, high-quality content.  The website provides value to the audience, therefore, it should be user-friendly, load fast, and easy to navigate.
  
  If you are new, here are some user-friendly AdSense-approved WordPress themes you can try :
  
  [Astra Pro](https://wpastra.com/)
  
  [Sahifa](https://themeforest.net/item/sahifa-responsive-wordpress-news-magazine-newspaper-theme/2819356)
  
  [GeneratePress](https://generatepress.com/)
  
  ### 2\. Important pages only
  
  The structure of the website plays a crucial role in getting approval. Your website must consist of an About Us page, a Privacy Policy page, and a Contact Us Page. These pages increase your website’s credibility and make your website look more genuine and legitimate. You should also remove irrelevant and low-value pages from your website, as they can lead to account rejection by AdSense.
  
  ### 3\. Website Navigation
  
  A clean and simple website layout and properly structured URLs help users to navigate through the website easily, plus it helps Google to identify it as a quality platform that is worth monetizing. You can follow the famous Silo Structure
  
  [Here](https://adsense.google.com/start/resources/platforms/) is the list of AdSense-approved platforms. You can compare these platforms with yours to figure out what’s missing.
  
  ### 4\. **Website** Maturity
  
  Even though there are no strict rules regarding the website’s existence, having an established online authority is definitely a great factor in improving your chances of approval. If you are new to the game, it is advisable to wait a minimum of six months before applying for Google AdSense. You can use this time to build a solid foundation, provide quality content, and bring more organic traffic to your website, which will come in handy in the near future.
  
  ### 5\. Sufficient High-Quality Content
  
  Content is the key to building credibility and trust. With high-quality, unique, valuable, and well-written content, your website stays active and relevant. You can choose different forms of writing and types of content to cover different aspects of your niche. In terms of articles and blogs, the word count should be around a minimum of 1000 words. Plus, your website must contain at least 30 to 40 articles before applying for Google AdSense approval.
  
  ### 6\. Organic Traffic is the Key
  
  If you want to earn [ad revenue](https://www.adpushup.com/blog/state-of-ad-revenue/), through Google AdSense, organic traffic plays a very important role. Organic traffic is purely based on how relevant your content is for your niche. Traffic comes directly from search engines, so you need to make sure that your content is attractive and visible to the audience. Organic traffic is an important consideration for advertisers who want to buy your ad inventory to show their ads.
  
  ### 7\. Update New Pages on Google Search Console
  
  If you want Google to discover your website, you need to index your website content in Google Search Console. This tool is a great way to keep track of the performance of your website and identify issues. Regularly monitoring and understanding your website vitals through Search Console can help you get AdSense approval fast.
  
  ## How to be eligible for AdSense?
  
  To qualify for AdSense approval, your website should adhere to Google’s policies, have valuable content and have organic traffic. Let’s understand some basic eligibility criteria to get AdSense approved.
  
  ### How much traffic is needed for AdSense?
  
  When it comes to traffic requirements, AdSense has not set up any minimum threshold that websites need to qualify to get AdSense approved. Moreover, it is preferred that your website has a good amount of traffic and valuable content. AdSense’s primary focus is the quality of the site in terms of user experience and relevance to your niche.
  
  So, this leads to another question: “Can I get AdSense approval without traffic?” Well, the answer is yes, technically AdSense has no minimum traffic requirement, but it does require a minimum level of authority to be approved. So, it is strongly recommended to focus on organic search traffic and building credibility of your website before applying for a Google AdSense account, because even if you have traffic, if the quality of content and website authority is poor, there is a high chance to be rejected.
  
  ### Content Requirements for Google AdSense
  
  Again, AdSense has not put any limit when it comes to content requirements on a website for the approval process, but you need to make sure that the available content on your website offers engaging information, is well researched, and most importantly, properly formatted to enhance readability. Plagiarised or duplicated content is a straight way to get rejected, so always make sure that the blogs and articles on your website are original and add value to your domain.
  
  Be consistent, and aim to cater for the needs of your audience. The website should be professional and offer a flawless user experience. To increase the domain authority of your website, you can focus on adding backlinks from trusted websites to boost traffic and increase ad impressions on your website.
  
  Finally, keep updating your content to ensure continued visibility on search engines. As discussed above, you should submit the newly added pages to Search Console to index them and signal Google that your website is genuine and trustworthy.
  
  ### Conditions for Google AdSense Approval
  
  AdSense approval requires meeting specific conditions set by Google AdSense.
  
  Let’s understand these conditions one by one:
  
  - Website ad inventory should be occupied with only relevant and engaging ads. Ads displayed on your website should be appropriate, well-aligned and properly placed for a better user experience.
  
  - Ad placement should be natural and non-disruptive. Navigation across the website should be easy and simple.
  
  - Your website should have organic traffic, i.e real visitors. You need to avoid “Artificial traffic” through bots and spamming
  
  - Adhering to Google AdSense requirements is non-negotiable i.e. be compliant with every Google policy.
  
  ## How to Apply for an AdSense Account (Google AdSense Approval Requirements)?
  
  Now that you know why AdSense bans publishers let’s move on to google AdSense approval requirements. Here’s how to apply for an AdSense account without getting banned:
  
  ### Step 1: Create Quality Content
  
  One of the most common mistakes people make is applying for AdSense without having enough high-quality content on their website. So it goes without saying, before you apply for Google Adsense, create content that resonates with your target audience and provides value.
  
  ### Step 2: Check AdSense Policies
  
  It must be emphasized more how important it is to follow Adsense policies if you want to apply for an account without the risk of getting banned. So, as mentioned earlier, you must adhere to the aforementioned AdSense policies. Thoroughly review the policies and confirm that your content does not breach any of the guidelines.
  
  ### Step 3: Getting Google Adsense Approval
  
  Now that you have been successful with AdSense policies, you can proceed to apply for a Google AdSense account. Here’s how you can do it:
  
  - Head to the [AdSense website](https://r.search.yahoo.com/_ylt=AwrPplaJZk5kius4.Vm7HAx.;_ylu=Y29sbwNzZzMEcG9zAzEEdnRpZAMEc2VjA3Ny/RV=2/RE=1682888458/RO=10/RU=https%3a%2f%2fadsense.google.com%2fstart%2f/RK=2/RS=fw_DGbiICAJCLWT6TVlA3ET8n2U-) and click on the “Sign up now” button.
  
  - Fill in the required details, such as your website URL, name, and email address.
  
  - Review the AdSense policies and agree to them by checking the box.
  
  - Lastly, click on the “Create account” button to submit your application.
  
  And there you are.
  
  Once you are done with the above-mentioned steps, Google will review your application and determine if your website meets the AdSense eligibility requirements. The review process may take several days, during which Google will examine your website’s content, traffic, and overall user experience.
  
  In case you get Google AdSense approval, you will receive an email notification.  You can then set up your AdSense account and start generating revenue from your website.
  
  Now that you know how to get Google AdSense approval, let’s have a look at the strategies you should follow to avoid getting banned from AdSense.
  
  ## Why Google AdSense Rejects a Website?
  
  A website can be rejected for many reasons, but the primary reason behind the account rejection is non-compliance with its policies and guidelines. Here are some common reasons why your AdSense application can be rejected. Let’s have a look:
  
  - Insufficient or low-quality content
  - Google Policy Violations
  - Lack of essential pages
  - Insufficient Traffic
  - Non-Indexed webpages
  - Fake or manipulated traffic.
  
  ## How to Get Your Rejected AdSense Account Approved
  
  To get your disapproved/ rejected account approved again, you need to make some necessary changes. Here’s what you can do:
  
  ### 1\. Review the Rejection Reason
  
  Google AdSense always provides a reason for disapproving the account by email. Common reasons include low-quality content, policy violations, insufficient traffic or non-indexed webpages. Read the email carefully to understand the issue.
  
  ### 2\. Fix Content and Compliance requirements
  
  Second, adhering to Google policies is a must if your content contains adult content or copyright violations; there is a higher chance of getting rejected. You should focus on creating original, high-quality, and valuable content for the audience. To boost credibility, ensure that pages like About Us, Privacy Policy, and Contact Us are present on the website.
  
  ### 3\. Work on Organic Traffic
  
  Don’t use artificial traffic sources like bots or spam clicks. Improve your organic traffic through SEO, keyword optimization, and regular updates to increase the visibility of your site and ensure regular visitors to the site.
  
  ### 4\. Optimize the Website Structure
  
  A clean and well-indexed website improves the chances of AdSense approval. Try to make your website mobile-friendly, easy to navigate and user-centric, remove excessive ads, broken links and slow-loading elements.
  
  ### 5\. Seek support from experts
  
  Sometimes getting approved by AdSense can be challenging. This is where seeking help from an expert can make a significant difference. Professionals who specialise in AdSense approval and monetization strategies can track down the critical issues and suggest the exact improvements your website needs. You can use AdSense [help centre](https://adsense.google.com/start/resources/contact-form/) or get in touch with specialists from platforms like [Upwork](https://www.upwork.com/hire/google-adsense-freelancers/), Fiverr, or [Codementors](https://www.codementor.io/google-adsense-experts)
  
  ## Key Takeaways
  
  ### (Quick Summary for the entire blog)
  
  - The website should have valuable and relevant content that engages users and complies with Google’s AdSense policies.
  - Your website should be user-friendly, fast loading, and easy to navigate. About us, privacy policy and contact us pages are very important to help with AdSense approval.
  - Websites that attract traffic organically have a high chance of AdSense approval.
  - Non-intrusive ad placement and a well-maintained website ensure a better user experience and approval odds.
  - Ensure the content is in line with Google’s policies. The website should be optimised to avoid any rejections.
  - Approval time can vary, but if your website meets all the requirements, the approval process can be done smoothly and faster.
  - Always avoid common reasons for which AdSense rejects the accounts, i.e low quality content, Google’s policy violation, missing essential pages, insufficient traffic, etc.
  - To fix a rejected AdSense account, review the rejection reason, fix content and compliance requirements, work on organic traffic, optimize the website structure, etc.
  - Adpushup provides advanced monetization solutions beyond AdSense for those seeking higher flexibility, earnings, and support.
  
  ## Frequently Asked Questions
  
  **1\. Who is eligible for Google AdSense?**
  
  To be eligible for Google AdSense, the publisher must be at least 18 years old, have a Google account, a website with high-quality, original content, and meet the AdSense program policies. Lastly, having an AdSense account and complying with AdSense policies are necessary.
  
  **2\. What are the requirements for AdSense approval?**
  
  A website or YouTube channel with original content, sufficient traffic, and compliance with AdSense policies.
  
  **3\. Can I reapply for AdSense if my application is rejected?**
  
  Yes, you can reapply once you have made the necessary changes to meet AdSense requirements.
  
  **4\. How to get AdSense approval easily?**
  
  To get AdSense approval quickly:
  
  – Your site must contain high-quality and original content
  
  – Your Website should be well-structured, easy to navigate, fast loading and in compliance with Google AdSense policies.
  
  – Avoid Your Money or Your Life niches as they significantly decrease your chances of getting approved.
  
  – Focus on Organic Traffic, the more the better.
  
