  # 12 Eligibility Criteria to Check Before Applying to AdSense
  
  - [April 27, 2022](https://growtraffic.co.uk/2022/04/27/)
  - ,[SEO](https://growtraffic.co.uk/category/search-engines/seo/seo-seo/)
  
  [Summarise this page in ChatGPT](https://growtraffic.co.uk/12-eligibility-criteria-to-check-before-applying-to-adsense/#)
  
  The [AdSense](https://growtraffic.com/blog/2019/10/eligibility-criteria-apply-adsense) programme that Google runs is a great way to make some extra money from a website, but there are many downfalls involved in this.
  
  ## **Google’s Official AdSense Eligibility Requirements**
  
  You can find the official list on the [AdSense](https://growtraffic.com/blog/2019/10/eligibility-criteria-apply-adsense) website, but this can also be scattered on other websites and forums, making it a bit harder to find.
  
  1. **You Must Be Over 18 Years of Age**
  
  As mentioned in Google’s terms and conditions document, to be able to utilise [AdSense](https://growtraffic.co.uk/12-eligibility-criteria-to-check-before-applying-to-adsense/12%20Eligibility%20Criteria%20to%20Check%20Before%20Applying%20to%20AdSense), you need to be over the age limit of 18 years old. You may also only have one account once you are in this age range.
  
  2. **You Must Own and Control Your Site**
  
  This is simple you need to be the person that has control of your website. [AdSense](https://growtraffic.co.uk/12-eligibility-criteria-to-check-before-applying-to-adsense/12%20Eligibility%20Criteria%20to%20Check%20Before%20Applying%20to%20AdSense) will not work if this is not the case, as they will not be able to access the primary source of your page.
  
  3. **Your Website Must Have Unique and Interesting Content**
  
  If Google finds your website and it is full of pages that haven’t got much detail on them.
  
  Or they have included content from other forums and websites, or that it won’t be that interesting for any of these readers or visitors, they will see no point in this being an [AdSense](https://growtraffic.co.uk/12-eligibility-criteria-to-check-before-applying-to-adsense/12%20Eligibility%20Criteria%20to%20Check%20Before%20Applying%20to%20AdSense) business.
  
  ![Google algorithm updates](<Base64-Image-Removed>)
  
  4. **Good Content Quality**
  
  Google has a tremendous experienced guide for all publishers.
  
  Ensure that you have excellent quality content on your website and check that the content you are putting out mentions some parts of the guide.
  
  Try not to get distracted by the non-popular sites showing [AdSense.](https://www.webnots.com/what-are-the-eligibility-criteria-for-google-adsense/)
  
  5. **Length Of Site Ownership**
  
  It was so much easier to get approved for [AdSense](https://www.webnots.com/what-are-the-eligibility-criteria-for-google-adsense/) back when it was first launched.
  
  But in today’s world, it is not an easy thing to be able to get AdSense approval from Google themselves.
  
  To ensure that your page is accurate and has the correct number of decent pages and content, Google has some restrictions on their main domain page.
  
  6. **Check Content Category**
  
  Google will not accept the work from [AdSense](https://www.webnots.com/what-are-the-eligibility-criteria-for-google-adsense/) websites that have a particular type of content, and these are.
  
  - Violent content
  - Dangerous content
  - Content that enables dishonest behaviour
  - Illegal content
  - Pages that will be offering compensation in their programmes
  
  ![Google images](<Base64-Image-Removed>)
  
  7. **Create a Privacy Policy for Your Blog**
  
  The first thing you will need to get the ball rolling when applying for Google [AdSense](https://www.webnots.com/what-are-the-eligibility-criteria-for-google-adsense/) and get the correct level of approval is to change the policy and privacy settings on your blog or website.
  
  If you need help with this, they can offer you that.
  
  8. **Set up a Contact Us Page**
  
  Make a contact us page, and if possible, also add your email that you will be using to apply for [AdSense](https://www.webnots.com/what-are-the-eligibility-criteria-for-google-adsense/).
  
  By creating this page, you are informing Google that you care a lot about your customers and clients and are ready to help them with any queries they might have.
  
  They are also able to contact us at any time.
  
  9. **Do Not Miss Any Important Pages**
  
  People who run WordPress websites have been rejected from [AdSense](https://shutterholictv.com/how-to-qualify-for-google-adsense/) because they have not included the essential pages needed.
  
  The pages include us, contact us, business privacy policies, terms, and conditions. Including these gives the website an official and professional look.
  
  This will boost the trust factors of your visitors and clients as it will make them feel like you are a trustworthy business and you know what you are talking about.
  
  10. **Using Top Level Domains**
  
  There has been a change to [AdSense’s](https://shutterholictv.com/how-to-qualify-for-google-adsense/) policy on Google. Suppose you are using a form of domain or a blogging site. It is not 100% certain that you will be approved.
  
  You need a high authority domain that you host by yourself; only then Google might look at your application.
  
